# Without this file git guesses per file and each developer's core.autocrlf
# setting decides the rest, so the same checkout differs between machines.

# Normalise line endings inside the repository. Working-tree endings still
# follow the platform, except where a rule below pins them deliberately.
* text=auto

# Shell scripts must stay LF wherever they are checked out. CI runs these on
# Ubuntu to build the AppImage and the .deb, and a CRLF shebang fails with
# "bad interpreter: No such file or directory" - a message that looks nothing
# like the line-ending problem it actually is.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Committed build output. Tailwind writes LF, and web/dist/styles.css is
# minified onto a single line, so a CRLF working copy reports the whole
# stylesheet as modified after every build.
*.css text eol=lf

# Never convert or attempt to merge these.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
